     zzccmmpp, zzddiiffff — compare compressed files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     zzccmmpp [_o_p_t_i_o_n_s] _f_i_l_e_1 [_f_i_l_e_2]
     zzddiiffff [_o_p_t_i_o_n_s] _f_i_l_e_1 [_f_i_l_e_2]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzccmmpp and zzddiiffff are filters that invoke cmp(1) or diff(1) respectively to
     compare compressed files.  Such files generally have a “Z” or “gz” exten‐
     sion (both the compress(1) and gzip(1) formats are supported).  Any
     _o_p_t_i_o_n_s that are specified are passed to cmp(1) or diff(1).

     If only _f_i_l_e_1 is specified, it is compared against a file with the same
     name, but with the extension removed.  When both _f_i_l_e_1 or _f_i_l_e_2 are spec‐
     ified, either file may be compressed.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
     TMPDIR  Directory in which to place temporary files.  If unset, _/_t_m_p is
             used.

FFIILLEESS
     /tmp/zcmp.XXXXXXXXXX   Temporary file for zzccmmpp.
     /tmp/zdiff.XXXXXXXXXX  Temporary file for zzddiiffff.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     cmp(1), compress(1), diff(1), gzip(1)

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     zzccmmpp and zzddiiffff rely solely on the file extension to determine what is, or
     is not, a compressed file.  Consequently, the following are not supported
     as arguments:

           --   directories
           --   device special files
           --   filenames indicating the standard input (‘-’)

